<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 22.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 22.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Feb 22</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     265	   0.97     492000 130.38    19.09</p>
<p>State Bank	   285	   1.02     447500 127.54    18.66</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   188	   0.69     543200 102.12    19.14</p>
<p>BSES		   235	   0.85     365490  85.89    18.86</p>
<p>MTNL		   230	   0.81     312800  71.94    18.36</p>
<p>ITC		    410	   1.53     145200  59.53    19.46</p>
<p>Tata Power	   132	   0.49     305150  40.28    19.36</p>
<p>ACC		   1445	   5.07	26310  38.02    18.30</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   920	   3.31	40150  36.94    18.76</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    240	   0.87     130100  31.22    18.90</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 18.88 percent on an annualised basis against 18.06 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Feb 15.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
